doc:home_1 a schema:Organization ;
    rdfs:label "the home"@en ;
    echr:hasExtractionNote "Government (in its memorial) stated that renovation work was carried out in late 2009 including sanitary facilities; the home now had central heating; the diet was varied and regularly included fruit and vegetables as well as meat; residents had access to television, books and games; the State provided them all with clothes — the applicant did not dispute these assertions."@en,
        "Residents did not have their own items of clothing because clothes were not returned to the same people after being washed."@en,
        "The applicant shared a room measuring 16 sq. m with four other residents; the beds were practically side by side."@en,
        "The home’s management kept hold of the applicant's identity papers and allowed him to leave only with special permission from the Director."@en .

